end, each pointing to a separate rounded rectangle representing a specific =
application. The left rectangle is labeled 'Reaching a Destination' and lis=
ts two sub-points: 'Jump to the End' and 'Gas Stations,' suggesting example=
s of problems solved using a greedy approach in this context. The right rec=
tangle is labeled 'Resource Allocation' and lists 'Candies' as an example p=
roblem.  The overall structure shows that 'Reaching a Destination' and 'Res=
ource Allocation' are both considered applications or examples of the broad=
